 good idea  I was wrong to support him for three  different reasons and most importantly  this is another way to actually back  handedly weaken Social Security and  Medicare and I want to go through each  of these reasons one by one so three  parts here number one the people who are  in the roughest shape right now are the  35-ish million people who lost their  jobs if you lost your job you're not  paying a payroll tax because you don't  have a job so seven point six five  percent tax holiday off the payroll tax  for people who aren't on any payroll is  not useful at all  second the people who do have jobs are  mostly earning the same amount of money  now I'm not saying they wouldn't love  not to pay this seven point six five  percent but you've got thirty five  million people that straight-up lost  their jobs so to them the payroll tax  holiday doesn't make a difference most  people fortunately for now are still  working and have not seen a decrease in  pay some people are still working but  have seen a decrease in pay but it is  not that many people the bulk of the  workers right now have not seen a  decrease in pay or are completely  unemployed and thus unaffected by a  payroll tax holiday and then number  three it is only a tax holiday this is  not a tax cut if you earn a hundred  thousand dollars for example in a year  that means in the second half of the  year you would expect to earn about  fifty thousand dollars for now saving  seven point six five percent puts thirty  eight hundred dollars back in your  pocket but it is only a tax holiday when  you file your taxes in 2021 and you  punch in how much you've paid for Social  Security and Medicare TurboTax or  whatever your accountant whoever will  spit out hey  that thirty eight hundred dollars you  didn't pay in the second half of 2020  you've got to pay it back in right now  because it was only a tax holiday so  doing this payroll tax cut would target  a relatively small group it would  deprive the government of nine hundred  and fifty billion dollars in revenue  through the end of the year it would  weaken Social Security and Medicare  which could then open the door to dirty  tricks from people like Trump and Larry  Kudlow and others to say hey we got to  do something with Social Security and  Medicare we don't have that much money  because of the tax  holiday you put in place and you've  still got to pay it back next year so we  can't let them do it I apologize that I  was supportive of this early on given  everything we now know I cannot in good  conscience support this and I'm sorry  that I suggested that it would have been  a good idea we're gonna continue  following this on Instagram our  instagram is david pakman show you can  also follow me on instagram personally  at david pakman we'll take a quick break  and be back right after this
 

